AI: ROOT CAUSE                                                                      

 • Faulty component: Pod grafana-7b9cbf56f5-qd4qp (part of the grafana          
   Deployment) in namespace astronomy‑shop                                      
 • Why it fails: The Grafana container attempts to bind to 0.0.0.0:8080. Port   
   8080 is already in use by multiple other services in the demo (e.g.,         
   checkout, cart, currency, etc.). The bind error ([Errno 98] address in use)  
   forces Grafana to repeatedly restart, producing connection‑refused errors    
   when it later tries to call its own HTTP API (localhost:3000). This is why   
   the pod shows 3 restarts and why the logs contain repeated ERROR and WARNING 
   entries about the address conflict and failed HTTP calls.                    
 • Evidence:                                                                    
    • Grafana pod status: restartCount: 3, ready: true (still running but       
      repeatedly restarted).                                                    
    • Logs (last hour, error‑filtered) contain:                                 
                                                                                
       [Errno 98] error while attempting to bind on address ('0.0.0.0', 8080):  
       address in use                                                           
       Retry... connection refused to                                           
       http://localhost:3000/api/admin/provisioning/...                         
                                                                                
    • Other services (checkout, cart, etc.) all expose containerPort: 8080,     
      confirming the port conflict.                                             

FIX                                                                             
Change Grafana’s HTTP port to a free value (e.g., the default 3000) by updating 
its Deployment/ConfigMap (or Helm values) to set GF_SERVER_HTTP_PORT=3000 (or   
remove any custom port setting). Then redeploy Grafana. This eliminates the bind
error, stops the restart loop, and restores the Grafana UI for the OpenTelemetry
demo.                                                                           

